## Project Overview

**CtrlAssist** is a Linux gaming accessibility tool that enables multiple physical controllers to operate as a single virtual input device. It provides:

- **Controller Multiplexing (mux)**: Combine two controllers (Primary + Assist) into one virtual gamepad
- **Controller Demultiplexing (demux)**: Split one controller to multiple virtual gamepads
- **System Tray Interface**: GUI for configuration via the desktop taskbar
- **Force Feedback**: Rumble pass-through from virtual to physical devices
- **Device Hiding**: Strategies to hide physical devices from games

### Technology Stack

| Dependency | Version | Purpose |
|------------|---------|---------|
| [gilrs](file:///home/ruffsl/git/ruffsl/CtrlAssist/src/utils/gilrs.rs#14-18) | ^0.11.1 | Gamepad input detection and events |
| [evdev](file:///home/ruffsl/git/ruffsl/CtrlAssist/src/utils/evdev.rs#159-170) | 0.13 | Linux event device creation/interaction |
| `clap` | ^4.5 | CLI argument parsing |
| `tokio` | 1.x | Async runtime for tray |
| `ksni` | ^0.3.3 | System tray (StatusNotifierItem) |
| [udev](file:///home/ruffsl/git/ruffsl/CtrlAssist/src/utils/hide.rs#239-246) | 0.9 | Device tree navigation for hiding |
| `notify-rust` | 4.11 | Desktop notifications |
| `serde`/[toml](file:///home/ruffsl/git/ruffsl/CtrlAssist/Cargo.toml) | 1/0.9 | Configuration serialization |

